    Large-Cap ETF' (2011) -- SAME ticker, SAME fund, SAME continuous price series. No data gap,
    no restatement. Does not affect this backtest.
  - The original 9 Select Sector SPDRs (1998) are structurally the oldest and most stable US
    sector-ETF family; XLRE (2015) and XLC (2018) were NEW launches following GICS sector splits,
    correctly excluded from the ranking pool before their real launch dates (see audit 7), not
    survivorship-biased inclusions.
  - Residual bias is 'universe selection', not 'individual fund survivorship': this backtest could
    not include a sector/asset-class ETF that was discontinued before 2026 and is unknown to this
    audit. For the specific instrument CLASS tested (large, liquid, well-known SPDR/iShares/
    Vanguard/Invesco funds), closures in this category are rare; no attempt was made to enumerate
    every historical closure, so this is SIZED as small but not zero, not proven zero.

